Below we discuss approaches to reduce the variance of Jˆ(θ; x1N , v1N1M ), which can lead to better performance in
practice. The most naïve approach, of course, is using a larger M to compute Jˆ(θ; x1N , v1N1M ). However, this requires more computation and when M is close to the data dimension, sliced score matching will lose its computational advantage over score matching.
